2. **Query 2 (UUID: 20260409192542) - InterWiki link renderer URL construction (8 results)**: InterWikiXHTMLLinkTypeRenderer.beginLinkExtraAttributes places `reference.getReference()` directly into the `href` anchor attribute without URL protocol validation. When an unknown interwiki alias is used (else branch, line 63), the raw reference is used as-is. When a known alias is found (if branch, lines 60-61), the reference is appended to the definition prefix. The XHTMLWriter only escapes HTML special characters, not URL protocols like `javascript:` or `data:`. An attacker can craft a wiki interwiki link with `javascript:alert(document.cookie)` as the reference path to inject XSS. Submitted as TRUE POSITIVE.
